  "activity": {
    "id": "act_vsepr-reduced-01",
    "name": "Reduced AR Lab: VSEPR from Lewis to Molecular Shape",
    "description": "A linear reduced AR walkthrough of VSEPR: determine steric number from a Lewis structure, map to electron-domain geometry, then apply lone pairs to obtain molecular geometry and bond-angle deviations. Each step activates a focused augmentation on a specific board/poster/settling stage.",
    "workplace": "vsepr-lab-01",
    "start": "a1_stericNumber",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "a1_stericNumber",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "1) Count steric number from a Lewis structure",
          "description": "Count electron domains around the central atom: bonding pairs + lone pairs. Their sum is the steric number, which determines the electron-domain geometry."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_domainBoard",
              "augmentation": "pred_stericNumberLabel",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "t1_click"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "a2_domainGeometry",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "2) Map steric number to electron-domain geometry",
          "description": "Use steric number to select the electron-domain geometry: 2 linear, 3 trigonal planar, 4 tetrahedral, 5 trigonal bipyramidal, 6 octahedral."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_geometryCards",
              "augmentation": "pred_domainGeometryCards",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "t2_detect"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "a3_lonePairsToMolecularShape",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "3) Convert electron domains to molecular shape",
          "description": "Molecular geometry depends on which domains are lone pairs. Lone pairs compress ideal angles and change the visible arrangement of atoms (molecular shape)."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_moleculeBoard",
              "augmentation": "pred_molecularShapesCards",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "t3_click"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "a4_minRepulsionSettle",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "4) Watch electron domains settle to minimum repulsion",
          "description": "Domains rearrange into the lowest-repulsion configuration predicted by VSEPR. Observe the geometry becoming stable as domains spread apart."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_settleStage",
              "augmentation": "pred_settleAnimation",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "t4_detect"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "a5_bondAngleDeviation",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "5) Explain lone-pair angle deviations",
          "description": "Lone pairs occupy more angular space than bonding pairs. This causes real bond angles to deviate from idealized values (e.g., water ~104.5\u00b0 vs methane ~109.5\u00b0)."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_anglePoster",
              "augmentation": "pred_angleDeviationVideo",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "t5_click"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "a6_audioReinforce",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "6) Reinforce the key idea (quick audio)",
          "description": "Lone pairs distort angles because they repel more strongly than bonding pairs; bond angles shift away from ideal VSEPR values."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
